25. Common Beginner Mistake
❌ Wrong
{isLoggedIn ? <Dashboard /> }

A ternary requires both sides:

condition ? trueResult : falseResult

So use:

{isLoggedIn ? <Dashboard /> : <Login />}

Or if you only need the true case:

{isLoggedIn && <Dashboard />}
26. Common Beginner Mistake — Changing State Directly

Don't do:

isLoggedIn = true;

If isLoggedIn is React state, use the setter:

setIsLoggedIn(true);

Why?

Because React needs to know that state changed.

❌ Direct assignment
isLoggedIn = true
       ↓
React isn't notified properly


✅ State setter
setIsLoggedIn(true)
       ↓
React schedules update
27. Common Beginner Mistake — Calling the Setter Immediately

Be careful with:

<button onClick={setIsLoggedIn(true)}>

This calls the function during rendering.

Instead:

<button onClick={() => setIsLoggedIn(true)}>

The arrow function says:

Execute this when the user clicks.

